use std
into codec_jpeg_enc.amni

Namespace codec_jpeg_enc; imports math. A baseline JPEG encoder (ITU-T T.81, JFIF), the counterpart of the decoder in codec_jpeg: 8-bit, three components (Y, Cb, Cr) with 4:2:0 subsampling (Y sampled 2 by 2, Cb and Cr 1 by 1 per 16 by 16 MCU), the standard quantization tables of Annex K.1 (luminance) and K.2 (chrominance) scaled for quality like the IJG library (quality q clamped to 1..100; scale = 5000 / q when q < 50, else 200 - 2 q; each entry `clamp((base * scale + 50) / 100, 1, 255)`), and the standard Huffman tables of Annex K.3 (DC luminance), K.4 (DC chrominance), K.5 (AC luminance) and K.6 (AC chrominance) as BITS and HUFFVAL lists exactly as printed in the standard (162 values for each AC table). All float-to-int conversions that truncate on purpose use `as!`.

`encode(rgba const byte[:], w int, h int, quality int, out byte[>..]&) bool` encodes a w by h RGBA image (alpha ignored) into out (cleared first); false when w or h is not positive or above 65535 or the input is shorter than `w * h * 4`. Write SOI (FF D8); a JFIF APP0 (FF E0, length 16, "JFIF" and a zero, version 1.1, density units 0, density 1 by 1, no thumbnail); DQT (FF DB) with table 0 (luminance) and table 1 (chrominance), 8-bit precision, entries in zigzag order; SOF0 (FF C0): precision 8, height, width, 3 components: id 1 sampling 0x22 table 0, id 2 sampling 0x11 table 1, id 3 sampling 0x11 table 1; DHT (FF C4) with the four tables (class 0 id 0 DC luminance, class 1 id 0 AC luminance, class 0 id 1 DC chrominance, class 1 id 1 AC chrominance); SOS (FF DA): 3 components (1: DC 0 AC 0, 2: DC 1 AC 1, 3: DC 1 AC 1), Ss 0, Se 63, Ah/Al 0; the entropy-coded data; EOI (FF D9). Marker segment lengths are big-endian and include their own two bytes.

Color: per pixel `Y = 0.299 R + 0.587 G + 0.114 B`, `Cb = -0.168736 R - 0.331264 G + 0.5 B + 128`, `Cr = 0.5 R - 0.418688 G - 0.081312 B + 128`. Pixels outside the image (for the last partial MCUs) repeat the nearest edge pixel. Chroma for each 2 by 2 pixel block is the mean of its four values. Each 8 by 8 block: subtract 128, forward DCT (the separable type-II DCT: `F(u, v) = 1/4 C(u) C(v) sum over x, y of f(x, y) cos((2x + 1) u pi / 16) cos((2y + 1) v pi / 16)`, C(0) = 1 / sqrt(2), else 1; precompute the 8 by 8 cosine table once), quantize by dividing by the table entry and rounding to the nearest integer (round half away from zero), then reorder to zigzag. MCU order: four Y blocks (top-left, top-right, bottom-left, bottom-right of the 16 by 16 area), then Cb, then Cr; MCUs left to right, top to bottom. Entropy coding (Annex F): build each table's code lengths and codes from BITS/HUFFVAL (canonical codes as in Annex C), DC coefficients as the difference from the previous block's DC of the same component (predictors start at 0), coded as size category plus the extra bits (negative values as `value - 1` in the low `size` bits); AC coefficients run-length coded with ZRL (0xF0) for 16 zeros and EOB (0x00) when the rest are zero. Bits are written most significant first into bytes; after every 0xFF data byte append a 0x00; at the end pad the last byte with 1 bits. Return true.
